going into the final run, with Russian " [:a {:href ""} "Aleksandr Tretyakov"] ", the 2008-09 World Cup champion and the bronze medalist at the 2009 World Championships, in third. But an outstanding time in the last run by Montgomery moved him ahead of Dukurs by 0.07 seconds to take the gold medal. Tretyakov did enough in his final run to hold on to his third place, 1.02 seconds behind Montgomery. In winning silver and bronze medals, Latvia and Russia won their first skeleton medals in the Olympics. Also noteworthy was the poor performance of the Germans " [:a {:href "/athletes/110443"} "Frank Rommel"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/119510"} "Sandro Stielicke"] ", who were second and third in the 2009-10 World Cup standings, but finished only seventh and 10th."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {} "Run #1"] [:th {} "Run #2"] [:th {} "Run #3"] [:th {} "Run #4"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/119499"} "Jon Montgomery"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CAN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CAN.png"}] "CAN"]] [:td {} "3:29.73"] [:td {} "52.60 (2)"] [:td {} "52.57 (1)"] [:td {} "52.20 (1)"] [:td {} "52.36 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/111080"} "Martins Dukurs"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/LAT"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/LAT.png"}] "LAT"]] [:td {} "3:29.80"] [:td {} "52.32 (1)"] [:td {} "52.59 (2)"] [:td {} "52.28 (2)"] [:td {} "52.61 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/110442"} "Aleksandr Tretyakov"]] [: